WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:04.819
If you want to hear my two fan theories about
the upcoming movie Glass, then stick around

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:08.500
to the end of this video.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.670
I just watched the trailer for Glass.

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:15.400
This has got to be my most anticipated movie
of all time.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.960
If this movie is good, this could be the greatest
trilogy ever.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:19.960
So.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.830
As you can imagine, I've got a lot to talk
about here.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:23.450
Please, do yourself a favor.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:26.900
Make sure you've seen these movies before
you watch this video.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:31.340
The trailer opens by introducing us to Dr.
Ellie Staple, a psychiatrist who specializes

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.180
in individuals who believe that they are superheroes.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.770
Now in Split, there a psychiatrist named Dr.
Fletcher, who works with The Horde.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:41.410
One of the many personalities asks Dr. Fletcher
what would happen to them if she were to pass

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.170
away, and this is her response.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.120
"If ever something were to happen to me, I've
made arrangements with a colleague from Baltimore

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.360
to take over."

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.410
What if this Dr. Staple is the colleague from
Baltimore?

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:56.670
The name of the asylum, as seen on this nametag
later in the trailer, is Raven Hill Memorial.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:00.850
Baltimore was the home of Edgar Allan Poe,
who wrote the famous poem The Raven, and of

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:03.110
course the NFL team, The Ravens, reside there.

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:07.111
But this movie does, like almost all of Shyamalan's
films including Split and Unbreakable, take

00:01:07.111 --> 00:01:08.500
place in Philadelphia.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.020
Next we see some shots from around the asylum,
including this one, from Kevin's room.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:14.200
You can tell because of the 24 toothbrushes.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.999
Also, at the beginning of this shot, the lights
are off and all we see are these three panes

00:01:17.999 --> 00:01:19.049
of glass.

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:21.319
That could come to represent the three main
characters.

00:01:21.319 --> 00:01:25.780
Not long after, we are shown those three characters:
all together in the same room.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.359
Perhaps the most shocking part though, is
that David Dunn is the only one who's chained

00:01:29.359 --> 00:01:30.359
up.

00:01:30.359 --> 00:01:32.759
The big question is going to be: what did
he do to become a criminal?

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:37.659
This could be a situation similar to The Incredibles,
where his acts of heroism also cause damage.

00:01:37.659 --> 00:01:41.210
Cause he does just kind of walk into people's
houses uninvited.

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:43.829
Later in the trailer this appears to be his
arrest scene.

00:01:43.829 --> 00:01:47.509
And then later on he seems to be surrendering,
and the removal of his raincoat is a symbol

00:01:47.509 --> 00:01:51.490
of him showing weakness during his arrest,
because in Unbreakable, water is essentially

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:52.490
is his Kryptonite.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:56.399
There's also this woman who's holding stop
signs, possibly David's wife, or possibly

00:01:56.399 --> 00:01:57.469
Doctor Staple.

00:01:57.469 --> 00:02:00.789
Back to this shot though, I'm guessing that
Elijah simply doesn't need to be chained up

00:02:00.789 --> 00:02:02.560
because he isn't a physical threat.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.259
But if they've now captured The Horde, you'd
think he would be chained up as well.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:09.320
Pay attention to the order they are sitting
in, because in the next shot, there are some

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.270
books propped up in the comic book store.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:14.150
The Legion of Regrettable Super Villains is
the book on the left.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.989
The League of Regrettable Superheroes on the
right and there’s something in the middle,

00:02:17.989 --> 00:02:20.790
I can't tell what book it is, but it probably
represents The Horde.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:23.000
There's also something off to the side here.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.879
If the bad guys are teaming up in this movie,
maybe David teams up with a new character

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:27.879
as well.

00:02:27.879 --> 00:02:31.940
For record, I don't consider Kevin to be a
bad guy, but out of the 24 personalities that

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:35.900
reside in his body, at least three of them
are bad and I think that's what Elijah refers

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.500
to when he says that line about the bad guys
teaming up.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.220
This scene is very reminiscent of the comic
store scene in Unbreakable where Elijah has

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.390
the epiphany about David Dunn having a weakness.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:48.670
The character in the comic he's looking at
has a resemblance to The Beast, the 24th personality

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:49.840
in Split.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:50.840
But with hair.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:54.349
This panel of him bending the bars is just
like The Beast bending the bars of the cage

00:02:54.349 --> 00:02:55.370
at the end of Split.

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:58.939
And just to break down this page, these two
are in some kind of danger when the beast

00:02:58.939 --> 00:03:00.610
guy comes in and grabs the bars.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.739
He says, "what they've done to us is unforgivable.

00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:07.390
I vowed to protect everyone from..." something...
it's too blurry to read at that point.

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:10.829
But then he breaks through the bars, the villain
says "time for me to get out of here", and

00:03:10.829 --> 00:03:13.580
the beast goes after these yellow eyes in
the dark.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:16.930
And his last quote is "I don't know how much
longer I can keep chasing him ..." I think

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.989
it's likely that we'll see a scene similar
to this in Glass.

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:24.299
Perhaps the character in this comic doesn't
represent The Beast, but rather David Dunn.

00:03:24.299 --> 00:03:28.400
If that's the case, maybe him breaking out
of the bars corresponds to this, and "I don't

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.879
know how much longer I can keep chasing him..."
refers to him getting older.

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:34.709
Before we move on from this page of comics,
they cut the trailer to make it look like

00:03:34.709 --> 00:03:39.090
Elijah Price is the one reading this comic,
but I don't think those are his hands.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:43.879
OK, this shot shows David Dunn in a diner
/ casino, and because I know people are going

00:03:43.879 --> 00:03:46.209
to ask, no it's not the same diner as the
end of Split.

00:03:46.209 --> 00:03:50.390
There is, however, a news report on the screen
showing something going down at Osaka Tower,

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:53.360
which I'm guessing is supposed to be a building
in Osaka, Japan.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:57.220
So I think Mr. Glass is up to his old tricks
again once he inevitably escapes.

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:58.370
Next shot.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.900
David bumps into this guy, whose face we can't
see at first.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:04.749
After a quick flashback of these chained up
cheerleaders, we see that it's Kevin... or

00:04:04.749 --> 00:04:07.180
at least one of the personalities, but which
one?

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.670
It could be Dennis, who is stated in Split
to have a thing for watching young girls dance

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:11.670
naked.

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:15.329
But it could be Hedwig, who is the owner of
that jacket and loves listening to music.

00:04:15.329 --> 00:04:17.010
OK, fine.

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:20.720
Roll it.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:28.230
Uh, Hedwig would probably be the only to wear
his headphones outside his hood like that.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:31.881
But if that is Hedwig, I guess that means
either Hedwig is complicit, like he was in

00:04:31.881 --> 00:04:36.140
the kidnapping of the girls in Split, or David
can see the actions of the entire Horde by

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:37.790
bumping into Kevin's body.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:41.230
By the way, the position that the girls are
chained up in almost looks to be a callback

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:44.070
to the way the Janitor tied up those girls
in Unbreakable.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:47.980
In Glass, we'll get to see a bunch of new
personalities that had files on the computer

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:53.350
in Split, but who never actually made an appearance
in the light, such as Mary Reynolds...

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.360
"I'm Mary Reynolds."

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.480
Someone who speaks Spanish...

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:57.480
"Por favor.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:58.480
Señor!"

00:04:58.480 --> 00:04:59.480
And apparently Logan Paul?

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:00.480
"We almost got you bro!"

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:04.640
When Mr Glass is talking about his brittle
bone disease, we see this X-Ray. from July

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:05.640
1999.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:09.450
Now Unbreakable came out in 2000 and could
take place in '99.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:13.160
This could be the very same X-Ray from that
fall down the stairs at the subway.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:17.010
However, I don't think that's the reason he's
still in a wheelchair now, because in Unbreakable,

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:20.480
the doctor tells him he'll be in the wheelchair
for a couple months and then be on crutches

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:21.480
after that.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:26.070
Split takes place 15 years after Unbreakable,
and I imagine Glass takes place shortly after

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:28.590
Split, because there is a brief shot later
in the trailer here where The Beast looks

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:31.070
to still have his gunshot wounds from Split.

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:35.440
Also, Mr. Glass’s crutches do make an appearance
at the end of the trailer, so maybe he won't

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:39.300
be wheelchair bound for the entirety of the
third one.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.300
Like some people.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.820
There's a brief shot in the trailer of a crowded
room, with almost no context, but if you pay

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:46.820
attention to this sign, you'll notice it's
a train station.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:51.170
Trains are significant in both films, in Unbreakable,
its David's survival of a train accident,

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:55.080
or I guess I should say train wreck, that
first gets Elijah's attention; and he also

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.930
searches for criminals by bumping into them
at the train station.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:01.080
In Split, the train yard is where Dennis goes
to unleash The Beast.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:04.260
And it's also mentioned that the root of his
disorder has something to do with his Dad

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:06.740
leaving on a train when he was very young.

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:10.180
Fan theory, I'm going to say that the train
his Dad was on was the same train derailed

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:12.210
at the beginning of Unbreakable.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:13.910
This is a very interesting shot.

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:17.140
At one point in the trailer we see Casey from
Split reaching out to the Horde.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:22.220
Here, we see her leaving the asylum with Elijah
Price's mom from Unbreakable, and David Dunn's

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:25.530
son Joseph Dunn, who is all grown up now.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:29.870
Could Joseph possibly be the owner of this
comic shop, whose face is conveniently hidden?

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:33.560
And as a side note, this character, whoever
he is, seems to be making a symbolic choice

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:35.340
between Heroes and Villains.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:38.020
That brings me to fan theory number two.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:39.020
Roll the clip.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:40.150
"May I meet The Beast?

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:43.300
I hope for your sake that he likes you.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:47.020
That sounds like the bad guys teaming up."

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:52.430
I think The Beast does end up liking Mr. Glass
for the same reason he likes Casey in Split,

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:56.270
because he is physically broken and the in
the eyes of The Beast, that makes him pure,

00:06:56.270 --> 00:07:03.160
unlike David, who is...

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:07.060
And speaking of Unbreakable, after this shot
where two nurses are running away from the

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:11.890
asylum and David Dunn can be seen in his raincoat
in the background, the trailer ends with imagery

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:13.930
of broken glass.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:15.900
Christmas is coming late this year.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.000
In January.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:20.390
I mean, technically that's next year, but
you get my point.

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:24.930
If you are stoked for this movie, if you are
ready to complete the Unbreakable trilogy,

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:27.550
let me know by leaving this video a like.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:30.430
Let me know your theories about Glass in the
comments.

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:34.460
"They say this one has a surprise ending."

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:38.880
And finally, if you're interesting in seeing
Things You Missed videos on Unbreakable, Split

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:43.890
and Glass, make sure you're subscribed to
